# Nix build outputs
result
result-*

# scaffold state (profiles, logs, caches)
.scaffold/

# generated by logos-module-builder at build time
generated_code/

# Rust build artefacts
target/

# The builder derives this from the trait in src/lib.rs on every build and
# stages it into its own copy of the crate. Committing a copy would recreate
# exactly the contract/code drift `codegen.rust.trait` exists to prevent —
# the .rs is the single source of truth (PLAN.md §2.2).
dialectica/rust-lib/generated/

# The logos-rust-sdk source, staged beside the crate so `cargo generate-lockfile`
# and `cargo test` can resolve the path dependency. Inside the Nix build the
# builder stages its own copy at the rev it pins; this one is a local
# convenience and must never be committed, or the checkout would pin an SDK the
# builder does not deliver.
#
# Stage it at the rev `dialectica/flake.nix` pins — read the rev from there
# rather than from this comment, because which SDK you get is a property of the
# builder pin (PHASE0-FINDINGS.md §2), and a stale rev here would quietly stage
# a different SDK than the build links against:
#
#   nix build github:logos-co/logos-module-builder/<rev from flake.nix>#rust-sdk-src \
#     -o dialectica/logos-rust-sdk-src
#
# `cargo test` cannot run without this: the path dependency is ungated, so
# cargo fails at manifest resolution before build.rs cfg gating can help.
dialectica/logos-rust-sdk-src

# editor / OS
*.swp
.DS_Store
.obsidian/

# generated by `lgs init`
.claude/
.cursor/
AGENTS.md

